\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The legal-route relation $R$ after the 260819 loop change, six rows, and the four laws the table makes checkable. The rows are deliberately NOT uniform: PROBE and EVIDENCE route only sideways or BACK to OUTLINE, so the single door out of the PREPARE loop is OUTLINE's own gate, four machine checks plus a person's \texttt  {approved:}. The judge alone reaches CLOSE and alone cannot reach itself, so every judged version passes through a producer before it is judged again; every phase without exception may stop at HOLD. The controller and the auditor encode this same table since 260819, keeping only a \textsc  {Compile} row no contract names, so already-stored receipts that name it stay auditable.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qpw1-route-relation}{{1}{1}{}{figure.1}{}}
